# t0936 — `.clone()` on a `Callable` is accepted by `gg check` and SEGVs at
# runtime. `Callable[T]` is in the single-owner carve-out and has NO clone path
# in the lowering (AGENTS.md "Ownership at Consuming Positions"), so this must
# be a CHECK-TIME REJECTION (Core #10, lower-or-reject) — never a crash.
#
# Reached by following the compiler's OWN advice: E_MoveWithoutOperator prints
# "write `^h` to move or `h.clone()` to copy" for single-owner types.
#
# INTENDED: rejected at check time with a diagnostic that does not offer
# `.clone()` for a type that has no clone path.
void main():
    Callable[int(int)] h = (int x): x + 1
    Callable[int(int)] g = h.clone()
    print(g(1))
